Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conclusion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9775359255386477`*^9, 
  3.977535927492813*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8fa93b39-5ef8-4df8-b0c2-\
f43f894f9a34"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] automates one of the \
most error-prone exercises in differential geometry: calculating the Riemann \
curvature tensor from scratch. \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s automation avoids the eager-expansion trap of student \
lore: \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[CapitalGamma] is not a tensor.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977536225547858*^9, 3.977536249271407*^9}, {
   3.977536308146929*^9, 3.977536341788349*^9}, {3.977536440174911*^9, 
   3.977536464833129*^9}, {3.9775364985199013`*^9, 3.977536523247518*^9}, {
   3.977536585051519*^9, 3.977536585130732*^9}, {3.977536656083826*^9, 
   3.977536656975308*^9}, {3.97753777534731*^9, 3.9775377902230377`*^9}, {
   3.977647534141658*^9, 3.97764770759956*^9}, {3.977678391232296*^9, 
   3.977678392274164*^9}, {3.977749895547062*^9, 3.97774997402324*^9}, 
   3.977777546325234*^9, {3.978092012016512*^9, 
   3.978092012365498*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c9b19f3-4c2e-4bda-8c85-\
2aaf4d7d71e6"],

Cell["\<\
Via the gamma-glue mechanism, \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s covariant derivative puts \[CapitalGamma] in a box and \
sends it inertly for later expansion in the ordinary product rule, ensuring \
correct derivative indices in comma notation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977536225547858*^9, 3.977536233678754*^9}, {
  3.9775365352774*^9, 3.977536572902362*^9}, {3.977536609106001*^9, 
  3.9775367219649477`*^9}, {3.977537799607901*^9, 3.977537828865676*^9}, {
  3.9775379782655888`*^9, 3.977538050535997*^9}, {3.977647717681651*^9, 
  3.977647796821754*^9}, {3.977678404035561*^9, 3.9776784163139753`*^9}, {
  3.977749991796399*^9, 
  3.977750048727523*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"12fe9c92-924d-4b89-82b0-\
880dd2fae2d7"],

Cell["\<\
The result is mathematically identical to the textbook definition, but is \
also structurally robust. Just reconfigure \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] \
for electromagnetism, Yang-Mills: any gauge theory.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977536225547858*^9, 3.977536233678754*^9}, {
  3.9775365352774*^9, 3.977536572902362*^9}, {3.977536609106001*^9, 
  3.9775368171608877`*^9}, {3.977536927314026*^9, 3.977536933186976*^9}, {
  3.977537869798625*^9, 3.977537870301622*^9}, {3.977538059606352*^9, 
  3.977538084338684*^9}, {3.9776478084514103`*^9, 3.9776478625759077`*^9}, {
  3.977750067348599*^9, 
  3.9777501219044724`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d5017b9d-6a43-4ab7-96a9-\
4c641b17ffe3"],

Cell["\<\
As a bonus, we illustrate compiling \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] \
notations onto MetricTensor and ChristoffelSymbol from the Wolfram Function \
Repository. This illustration is a proof-of-concept for a full compiler \
backend for \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977678434748913*^9, 3.9776784633757763`*^9}, {
  3.9776786604240303`*^9, 3.9776787268859367`*^9}, {3.97775013388129*^9, 
  3.977750158161399*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ce7d85c-280b-46b1-8a21-\
0b0a1494db40"],

Cell["\<\
In future work, we will continue to extend and expand \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] for more applications in relativity and gauge theory.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977536225547858*^9, 3.977536233678754*^9}, {
  3.9775365352774*^9, 3.977536572902362*^9}, {3.977536609106001*^9, 
  3.977536919360814*^9}, {3.9775381069611588`*^9, 3.9775381279403143`*^9}, {
  3.977647871321611*^9, 
  3.97764790291636*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b1d419f6-e013-49ca-99ba-\
6dd037955c2c"]
}, Open  ]],

